    "explanation": "Implements the staged numeric controller. Draft edits are independent from the committed lattice value; commits validate ASCII signed decimal safe integers and snap to the nearest legal value, resolving ties downward. Steps move by one lattice position with endpoint clamping, cancel restores the committed value, and disabled mode blocks only input, commit, and step.",
    "program": "function solve({config,state,event}){let s=state;if(s===null)s={v:config.initial,d:String(config.initial),e:null,x:false,min:config.min,max:config.max,step:config.step};let t=event.type;if(t==='mode')s.x=event.disabled;else if(t==='cancel'){s.d=String(s.v);s.e=null}else if(!s.x&&t==='input'){s.d=event.text;s.e=null}else if(!s.x&&t==='commit'){let ok=/^[+-]?\\d+$/.test(s.d),n=ok?Number(s.d):NaN;if(!ok||!Number.isSafeInteger(n))s.e='invalid';else{let q=Math.floor((s.max-s.min)/s.step),k=Math.floor((n-s.min)/s.step);if(k<0)k=0;if(k>q)k=q;let a=s.min+k*s.step,b=k<q?a+s.step:a;if(k<q&&Math.abs(n-a)>Math.abs(b-n))a=b;s.v=a;s.d=String(a);s.e=null}}else if(!s.x&&t==='step'){let q=Math.floor((s.max-s.min)/s.step),k=(s.v-s.min)/s.step+(event.direction<0?-1:1);if(k<0)k=0;if(k>q)k=q;s.v=s.min+k*s.step;s.d=String(s.v);s.e=null}return{state:s,output:{value:s.v,draft:s.d,dirty:s.d!==String(s.v),error:s.e,disabled:s.x}}}"
